Mostly by testing for different components of intelligence, like verbal
and spatial.  Verbal IQ would be expected to correlate more with
cultural bias than spatial IQ.  Use the verbal scores to track cultural
influences to filter out the intrinsic culture-free effects on the
spatial (and other) scores.  Same with other environmental influences
like quality of education etc.

The references to Jensen I gave are the only place where I've seen this
approach rigorously applied.  However I'm not an expert....

